# Regular-sequence descent through a flat quotient square

@stack 02JP

The regular-sequence predicates and the canonical closed fiber are owned by
`Ideal.IsGeneratedByRegularSequence` and `Ideal.Fiber`.  This file retains the
source-facing descent statement for a flat square of quotient maps.
-/

@[expose] public section

/- Lemma 10.135.12 (02JP): let `R → S` be a flat local homomorphism.  Suppose
`R` and its closed fiber are regular local rings, `J` and its image in the
closed fiber are generated by regular sequences, and the compatible quotient
map `R ⧸ I → S ⧸ J` is flat.  Then `I` is generated by a regular sequence. -/
